<% content_for :title, "On Stigma | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-stigma-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-stigma-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-stigma-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-stigma-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / ON STIGMA
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>THEY DON'T</span>
        <span>KNOW THE</span>
        <span>WHOLE FUCKING STORY.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-stigma-intro">
        LABELS. ASSUMPTIONS. SHAME.<br>
        AND OTHER PEOPLE THINKING<br>
        THEY KNOW WHO YOU ARE.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- WHAT STIGMA DOES -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-pink">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      01 / STIGMA
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        ONE WORD.<br>
        WHOLE FUCKING<br>
        STORY.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Bipolar. Addict. Alcoholic. Sober. Mentally ill.
      </p>

      <p>
        A label can describe something real without describing
        everything about the person carrying it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Stigma happens when people take one piece of information
        and use it to write the rest of your story for you.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-callout">
        <p>
          A DIAGNOSIS CAN DESCRIBE SOMETHING ABOUT YOU.<br>
          IT DOESN'T GET TO DESCRIBE ALL OF YOU.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ASSUMPTIONS -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-yellow">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      02 / ASSUMPTIONS
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        PEOPLE LOVE<br>
        FILLING IN<br>
        THE BLANKS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Once somebody knows a diagnosis or a history,
        everything can suddenly get interpreted through it.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-thoughts">

        <p>"YOU'RE UPSET? MUST BE THE BIPOLAR."</p>
        <p>"YOU'RE EXCITED? ARE YOU MANIC?"</p>
        <p>"YOU HAD AN ADDICTION? CAN I TRUST YOU?"</p>
        <p>"YOU DON'T DRINK? WHAT HAPPENED?"</p>
        <p>"YOU TAKE MEDICATION? ARE YOU OKAY?"</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        Sometimes people are genuinely trying to understand.
        Sometimes they're ignorant. Sometimes they're scared.
        Sometimes they're just being assholes.
      </p>

      <p>
        Their assumption is still not automatically a fact.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- INTERNALIZED STIGMA -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-purple">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      03 / INTERNALIZED STIGMA
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHEN THEIR<br>
        VOICE BECOMES<br>
        YOURS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The nastiest version of stigma isn't always somebody saying
        something shitty to you.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes you've heard the message enough that you start
        saying it to yourself.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">STIGMA SAYS</p>
          <p>I'M FUCKED UP.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">REALITY</p>
          <p>I'M DEALING WITH SOME FUCKING HARD THINGS.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">STIGMA SAYS</p>
          <p>MY PAST PROVES WHO I AM.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">REALITY</p>
          <p>MY PAST IS PART OF MY STORY, NOT THE END OF IT.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- SHAME -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-black">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      04 / SHAME
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        I DID<br>
        SOMETHING<br>
        VS. I AM SOMETHING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        There's a difference between taking responsibility for something
        and turning it into your identity.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-compare">

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">ACCOUNTABILITY</p>
          <p>I DID SOMETHING THAT HURT ME OR SOMEONE ELSE.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">SHAME</p>
          <p>I AM A BAD PERSON.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Accountability gives you somewhere to go:
        acknowledge it, repair what you can, learn something,
        change your behavior.
      </p>

      <p>
        Shame just keeps pointing at you and saying,
        "See? This is what you fucking are."
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-callout">
        <p>
          YOU CAN OWN WHAT YOU DID<br>
          WITHOUT BECOMING WHAT YOU DID.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- DISCLOSURE -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-pink">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      05 / DISCLOSURE
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHO GETS<br>
        TO KNOW<br>
        YOUR SHIT?
      </h2>

      <p>
        You don't owe every person you meet your complete medical,
        psychiatric, addiction, or recovery history.
      </p>

      <p>
        Disclosure can be useful, connecting, necessary, or freeing
        in some situations. In others, privacy is completely reasonable.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-question-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Why do I want to tell this person?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>What do they actually need to know?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Have they shown that they can handle personal information responsibly?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>What am I hoping will happen after I tell them?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Am I comfortable if their reaction isn't the one I want?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="stigma-callout">
        <p>
          PRIVACY IS NOT THE SAME<br>
          FUCKING THING AS SHAME.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BIPOLAR -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-yellow">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      06 / BIPOLAR STIGMA
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOU'RE NOT<br>
        EVERY FUCKING<br>
        STEREOTYPE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Bipolar disorder gets flattened into caricatures:
        unpredictable, unstable, dramatic, dangerous,
        impossible to trust, impossible to understand.
      </p>

      <p>
        A diagnosis can help explain patterns of symptoms.
        It does not automatically explain every emotion,
        argument, opinion, decision, personality trait,
        or bad fucking day.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-big-question">
        IS THIS ACTUALLY<br>
        ABOUT MY DIAGNOSIS —<br>
        OR DID SOMEBODY JUST<br>
        DECIDE EVERYTHING IS?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ADDICTION -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-purple">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      07 / ADDICTION STIGMA
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOUR WORST<br>
        PERIOD ISN'T<br>
        YOUR WHOLE LIFE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Addiction can leave behind consequences.
        Some of them don't disappear just because you're sober.
      </p>

      <p>
        Recovery doesn't require pretending the past didn't happen.
        But neither does accountability require permanently freezing
        yourself as the person you were at your worst.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-callout">
        <p>
          RECOVERY MEANS CHANGE IS POSSIBLE.<br>
          OTHERWISE WHAT THE FUCK<br>
          WOULD WE BE DOING HERE?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- OTHER PEOPLE -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-black">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      08 / OTHER PEOPLE
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHO GETS<br>
        A FUCKING<br>
        VOTE?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Not every opinion deserves equal weight.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-vote-grid">

        <div>
          <h3>THEY MIGHT GET A VOTE.</h3>

          <p>They actually know you.</p>
          <p>They want you well.</p>
          <p>They tell you difficult things respectfully.</p>
          <p>They understand the situation.</p>
          <p>Their feedback helps you see something useful.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>THEY MIGHT NOT.</h3>

          <p>They barely know you.</p>
          <p>They're operating from stereotypes.</p>
          <p>They're trying to shame you.</p>
          <p>They refuse to acknowledge change.</p>
          <p>They're committed to misunderstanding you.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="stigma-big-question">
        WHY AM I HANDING<br>
        THIS PERSON THE PEN<br>
        TO WRITE MY FUCKING STORY?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- RESPONDING -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-pink">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      09 / RESPONDING
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOU DON'T<br>
        HAVE TO GIVE<br>
        A TED TALK.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Sometimes you want to educate somebody.
        Sometimes you want to correct them.
        Sometimes you want to explain.
      </p>

      <p>
        And sometimes the correct response is absolutely fucking nothing.
      </p>

      <div class="stigma-response-grid">

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">CORRECT IT</p>
          <p>"That's not actually what bipolar disorder means."</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">BOUNDARY</p>
          <p>"I'm not discussing my diagnosis with you."</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">CLARIFY</p>
          <p>"Are you asking me, or are you assuming?"</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="stigma-label">EXIT</p>
          <p>"I'm done with this conversation."</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        You get to decide whether a conversation deserves your energy.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CHECK YOUR OWN STORY -->
  <section class="stigma-section stigma-section-yellow">

    <div class="stigma-section-number">
      10 / CHECK YOUR OWN STORY
    </div>

    <div class="stigma-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHAT HAVE<br>
        YOU STARTED<br>
        BELIEVING?
      </h2>

      <div class="stigma-question-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What labels do I use against myself?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Whose voice do those labels sound like?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>What do I believe my diagnosis says about me?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>What do I believe my addiction history says about me?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Am I confusing consequences with identity?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>What evidence exists that I've changed?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>07</span>
          <p>What would I say to somebody else with my exact history?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="stigma-ending">

    <p class="stigma-ending-small">
      YOU ARE ALLOWED TO BE MORE COMPLICATED THAN THE LABEL.
    </p>

    <h2>
      OWN YOUR SHIT.<br>
      NOT THEIR<br>
      FUCKING STORY.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Take responsibility for what belongs to you.
      Keep learning. Keep changing. Keep recovering.
      And stop carrying every assumption somebody else tries to hand you.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "stigma-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>